```python
class Animal:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name

    def speak(self):
        return '...'


class Dog(Animal):
    def __init__(self, name, breed='mutt'):
        super().__init__(name)
        self.breed = breed

    def speak(self):
        return 'Woof'
```

Call `super().__init__(...)` so the parent sets its own attributes. Prefer composition over deep hierarchies; two levels is usually enough.

